WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.167
Let's walk through this proof: Irrationality of √2.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.150
Suppose √2 is rational.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.127
Square both sides.

00:00:11.127 --> 00:00:13.880
Squaring both sides of the equation.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.883
a must be even.

00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:19.740
Since a² is a multiple of 2, a must be even.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.140
Substitute a = 2k.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:28.740
Substitute a = 2k into a² = 2b².

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.240
Simplify to find b.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.721
b must also be even.

00:00:33.721 --> 00:00:37.860
Since b² is a multiple of 2, b must be even.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.723
But they can't both be even!

00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:44.118
If both are even, they share a factor of

00:00:44.118 --> 00:00:47.512
2, so the fraction was not in lowest terms.

00:00:47.512 --> 00:00:50.530
So, in summary: The proof is a standard

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.170
and correct application of proof by contradiction.
